 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 04 - Loading IQ Data from Files\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook teaches how to load raw IQ sample data from binary files into NumPy arrays."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Generating a Dummy IQ File\n",
    "\n",
    "In practice, IQ data comes from SDR hardware or simulators. Here we create a small binary file to work with."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create a synthetic IQ file: interleaved float32 I/Q\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "n_samples = 2048\n",
    "t = np.linspace(0, 1, n_samples)\n",
    "iq = (1.0 + 0.5j) * np.exp(2j * np.pi * 100 * t) + 0.1 * (np.random.randn(n_samples) + 1j * np.random.randn(n_samples))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save as interleaved float32: [I0, Q0, I1, Q1, ...]\n",
    "interleaved = np.zeros(2 * n_samples, dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "interleaved[0::2] = iq.real\n",
    "interleaved[1::2] = iq.imag\n",
    "interleaved.tofile('dummy_iq.bin')\n",
    "print(f\"Created dummy_iq.bin with {len(interleaved)} float32 values ({len(interleaved) * 4} bytes)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Reading with `np.fromfile`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Read raw interleaved data\n",
    "raw = np.fromfile('dummy_iq.bin', dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "print(f\"Raw array shape: {raw.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Raw array dtype: {raw.dtype}\")\n",
    "print(f\"First 10 values: {raw[:10]}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Interleave-to-Complex Conversion"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Reshape into [I, Q] pairs then convert to complex\n",
    "iq_pairs = raw.reshape(-1, 2)\n",
    "iq_complex = iq_pairs[:, 0] + 1j * iq_pairs[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"IQ complex shape: {iq_complex.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"IQ complex dtype: {iq_complex.dtype}\")\n",
    "print(f\"First 5 samples:  {iq_complex[:5]}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Validating the Load"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(f\"Number of samples: {iq_complex.shape[0]}\")\n",
    "print(f\"dtype: {iq_complex.dtype}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Mean I: {np.mean(iq_complex.real):.6f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Mean Q: {np.mean(iq_complex.imag):.6f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Min magnitude: {np.min(np.abs(iq_complex)):.6f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Max magnitude: {np.max(np.abs(iq_complex)):.6f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Mean power:    {np.mean(np.abs(iq_complex)**2):.6f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Common Loading Mistakes\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Wrong dtype**: Reading `float32` data as `int16` produces garbage.\n",
    "2. **Forgetting interleave**: Reading as `complex64` directly from interleaved data gives wrong values.\n",
    "3. **Wrong byte order**: On some systems, big-endian vs. little-endian matters."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Mistake 1: wrong dtype\n",
    "raw_wrong = np.fromfile('dummy_iq.bin', dtype=np.int16)\n",
    "print(f\"Wrong dtype (int16): shape={raw_wrong.shape}, first 10: {raw_wrong[:10]}\")\n",
    "print(\"These values look wrong!\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Mistake 2: no interleave conversion\n",
    "raw_no_deinterleave = np.fromfile('dummy_iq.bin', dtype=np.float32)\n",
    "print(f\"\\nWithout deinterleave: shape={raw_no_deinterleave.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"This is NOT complex data yet.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Correct way\n",
    "def load_iq_from_interleaved(filename, dtype=np.float32):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Load interleaved I/Q binary file and return complex array.\"\"\"\n",
    "    raw = np.fromfile(filename, dtype=dtype)\n",
    "    if raw.size % 2 != 0:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"Odd number of values ({raw.size}), cannot form I/Q pairs.\")\n",
    "    iq_pairs = raw.reshape(-1, 2)\n",
    "    return iq_pairs[:, 0] + 1j * iq_pairs[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "iq_loaded = load_iq_from_interleaved('dummy_iq.bin')\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded: shape={iq_loaded.shape}, dtype={iq_loaded.dtype}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Matches original: {np.allclose(iq_loaded, iq)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
